"comparison": "Both MS and BAC identify the commercial real estate (CRE) office portfolio as a primary driver of credit losses, but they differ in the nature of the impact described. MS reports that its allowance remained relatively unchanged, with CRE office charge-offs offset by improved macroeconomic outlooks and specific CRE provisions (ms_2024_7_P333_S001). In contrast, BAC reports a significant increase in net charge-offs ($6.0 billion vs $3.8 billion), explicitly attributing this rise to the commercial real estate office portfolio alongside credit card loans, indicating a more severe deterioration in that segment compared to MS's offsetting dynamics (bac_2024_7_P384_S002, bac_2024_7_P384_S004).",
