"comparison": "Both MS and Citi disclose the determination and composition of the Allowance for Credit Losses (ACL), but they differ in the level of structural detail provided. MS outlines the risk factors considered in determining the allowance, such as borrower financial strength, LTV ratio, and qualitative economic conditions (ms_2024_7_P332_S002, ms_2024_7_P332_S003). Citi, however, defines the ACL by its component balance sheet line items, specifically distinguishing between reserves for funded loans (ACLL) and unfunded lending commitments (ACLUC), whereas MS discusses the factors influencing the aggregate allowance without this structural breakdown in the cited text (c_2024_7_P680_S001, c_2024_7_P680_S003).",
